\\# Module linker
\\# Links required object files together by searching for VC.unresolved()
\\# Requires a list of vco files in the current PATH, provided by cli wrapper
\\#
\\# Returns a vcx file with a single VC.run() call
\\#
\\# run with <input_file> <output_file> <module_list>
\\#
\\# Module list should be lines of 
\\# <namespace> <path>
\\# for example:
\\# local: /path/to/module.vco 
\\# std: /path/to/module.vco

\\ Copy the source buffer into the output buffer
\\ Done before any macros are loaded to make sure the input file doesn't
\\ have any changes which would fail ZZ for the output file
gg0vG$y

VG"_d
p

\\# Macro @p: Format modules buffer for error handling
\\#
\\# Requires:
\\#   - Current window must be modules
\\#
\\# Effects:
\\#   - Adds an empty line after every module.
\\#   - Prepends a counter for expansion-depth counter and mark as 'r'
\\#   - Adds conditionals match anchors to increment the counter or reset it
\\#     back to zero based on type of module, i.e., root or indirect
\\# 
\\# Notes:
\\# Add a line "root" below initial module requirements to differentiate them
\\# from the modules added indirectly through the expansion.
\\# In the object file a VC.unresolved() can only be followed by another VC call
\\# or EOF, so the next line can be used to anchor searches. Copy the first 
\\# three characters of the line below (j"ty3l) and search using ?^Rt.
\\# Execute the macro after the search anchor word to increment or reset counter.
o
