\\# Macro @y(@n, @f, @t): Search for a module and copy its contents.
\\#
\\# Inputs:
\\#   - @f: Module name.
\\#   - @n: Namespace.
\\#   - @t: First three characters of the line following the module reference.
\\#
\\# Requires:
\\#   - Current window is the modules buffer.
\\#   - Modules buffer has been initialised for linker processing.
\\#
\\# Effects:
\\#   - Module content without the lua << EOF header & EOF footer stored in @".
\\# 
\\# Failures:
\\#   - Module is not a valid object file.
\\#   - Module cannot be found in the module search path.
\\#   - Maximum expansion depth (50) is exceeded.
\\#
\\# Error Handling:
\\#   - Delegates object file validation to @a which uses @h to set quit macro
\\#     in case of failure.
\\#   - Missing module and expansion-depth exceptions result in a direct quit
o
