\\# Macro @m - Recursive substitution of VC.unresolved() references with module
\\#
\\# Requires:
\\#   - Current window is the input file
\\#   - Input file and modules exist in a horizontal split where modules is above
\\#     input file
\\#   - Modules buffer is prepared for linker processing
\\#   - Every module reference is the initial input file must have a "root" line
\\#     marker below it
\\#
\\# Effects:
\\#   - All VC.unresolved() references are replaced with VC.run() recursively
\\#
\\# Failures:
\\#   - Module doesn't exist in PATH
\\#   - Maximum expansion depth (50) violated
\\#   - Some module reference isn't a valid object file
\\#
\\# Error Handling:
\\#   - @a (assert for valid object file) sets @h to a quit macro if a required
\\#     module isn't a valid object file. @h must be called after the entry macro
\\#     to ensure correct error handling in case of an error.
o
  agg
  a/^VC.unresolved(\"\zs.*\")
  ajk
  amfk
  a/^VC.unresolved(\"\zs[^:]*\")
  ailocal:
  a`f
  a"ndf:
  a"fyi"
  aj0"ty3l
  ak
  a@y
  aj
  a'f
  a"_dd
  aP
  aGciWVC.unresolved("a")
  a@m
